WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.800
In 2018, chances are that everyone has multiple
favorite Netflix movies and TV shows.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:10.660
And it's also a safe bet that everyone is
super excited for upcoming Netflix originals

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.200
that are arriving on a wave of hype.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.600
But with so much new content added to the
streamer every day, it's impossible to keep

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.600
track of everything.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:22.020
Thus, some future movies and shows have fallen
under the radar even though they actually

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.700
feature big stars and buzzworthy premises.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.660
Let's take a closer look at upcoming Netflix
originals that nobody is talking about…yet.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.220
The Chilling Adventures of Sabrina

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:39.050
Riverdale executive producer Roberto Aguirre-Sacasa
is bringing Sabrina the Teenage Witch to Netflix,

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:41.880
although she won't be anything like Melissa
Joan Hart's version.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:46.300
This version is based on the comic series
Chilling Adventures of Sabrina, which tells

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.600
a dark origin story for the witchy teen.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:53.680
The show follows Sabrina, played by Mad Men's
Kiernan Shipka, as she tries to balance being

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:57.340
half-witch and half-mortal while fighting
against evil forces.

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:02.360
Chilling Adventures already has a two-season,
20-episode order, so expect quite a lot of

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:06.140
magical mishaps in Greendale after it premieres
on October 26th.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:08.820
And, hopefully, a Riverdale crossover or two.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:11.120
Russian Doll

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:15.740
Natasha Lyonne has already had success with
a Netflix hit, earning an Emmy nomination

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:17.680
for her work on Orange is the New Black.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:21.680
She's set to team up with the streamer once
again for Russian Doll, which she co-created

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:25.460
with Amy Poehler and Sleeping With Other People
director Leslye Headland.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:29.979
The eight-episode series stars Lyonne as a
young woman named Nadia who, throughout one

00:01:29.979 --> 00:01:34.500
endless night, serves as the guest of honor
at a "seemingly inescapable party."

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.909
The show has been described as "an ambitious
and uniquely formatted comedy that will have

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:40.920
viewers guessing as much as they will be laughing."

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:45.280
With that description and the incredibly talented
cast, this is shaping up to be one of your

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:46.480
new favorite shows.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.400
The Eddy

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:52.620
La La Land director Damien Chazelle is getting
back into the musical game.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:56.880
The Oscar winner is set to executive produce
and direct two episodes of the musical drama

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:00.780
series The Eddy, which is set in modern-day,
multicultural Paris.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:05.040
It will revolve around a jazz club with American
and French-Arab co-owners.

00:02:05.049 --> 00:02:09.190
The show will tell the story of "a club, its
owner, the house band, and the chaotic city

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:10.140
that surrounds them."

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.920
The Eddy will be shot in France with dialogue
in French, English, and Arabic.

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:19.220
The eight-episode series also has BAFTA Award-winning
writer Jack Thorne on board, as well as Grammy

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:22.640
Award-winning composer Glen Ballard writing
the original score.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.100
Dolly Parton anthology

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.560
Dolly Parton is one of the greatest songwriters
who's ever lived.

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:32.000
She's had a hand in penning almost all of
her most memorable hits, including "I Will

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.420
Always Love You," "9 to 5," "Coat of Many
Colors," and "Jolene."

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:40.580
She has a knack for composing songs that feel
like real people are singing about real situations,

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:43.580
and Netflix is going to turn some of those
into narrative films.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:48.430
In 2018, the service announced plans for an
eight-part anthology series, in which each

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:52.310
episode will be a self-contained story based
on one of Parton's tunes.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:53.980
In a press statement, the singer said,

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.440
"We hope our show will inspire and entertain
families and folks of all generations."

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:02.680
Parton will executive produce the series as
well as briefly appear in a few episodes.

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:04.680
Sunshine Scouts

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:10.220
After more than a decade creating hit shows
for ABC, television juggernaut Shonda Rhimes

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:14.620
signed a deal in April 2018 to bring her "Shondaland"
brand to Netflix.

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:19.160
Three months later, the prolific Rhimes announced
that she and her crew were at work on a whopping

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:24.170
eight different series, including dramas,
documentaries, and even a pitch black half-hour

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:26.230
comedy called Sunshine Scouts.

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:31.660
Overseen by Rhimes but created by writer/actress
Jill Alexander, the series takes place after

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:36.880
an event of apocalyptic proportions destroys
a great deal of civilization and life on Earth.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:41.220
A group of teenage girl scouts at a summer
camp have to band together to thrive in this

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:42.180
brave new world.

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:46.980
They abide by "Sunshine Scout Law" and use
their many scouting skills to find food and

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:49.360
shelter and avoid nuclear fallout.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:51.830
Norm Macdonald Has a Show

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:56.800
Finally, Norm Macdonald, arguably the greatest
talk show guest ever, will host his own talk

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:57.300
show.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:02.080
The one-of-a-kind comedian will soon be inviting
guests to talk to and mock, as Norm Macdonald

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:04.300
Has a Show premieres September 14th.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:09.000
Following David Letterman, Chelsea Handler,
and Michelle Wolf, Macdonald joins the Netflix

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.480
lineup of late-night talk shows you can watch
anytime.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:16.759
He'll be a co-showrunner in addition to hosting,
and his sidekick will be Adam Eget, his co-host

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:18.500
on the Norm Macdonald Live podcast.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:23.530
The initial guest lineup includes Drew Barrymore,
David Spade, Judge Judy, David Letterman,

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:28.520
Jane Fonda, Chevy Chase, M. Night Shyamalan,
Michael Keaton, Billy Joe Shaver, and Lorne

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.020
Michaels.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:30.920
Turn Up Charlie

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:35.740
After stepping away from the small screen
for a while to appear in multiple movie franchises,

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:40.460
Idris Elba will return to television with
an edgy comedy called Turn Up Charlie.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:44.780
He co-created the show, and it's about a topic
close to his heart: electronic music.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:50.580
Elba's a DJ in real life, and the show is
about an aging bachelor and EDM DJ who agrees

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:54.560
to be a caretaker for his celebrity best friend's
obnoxious young daughter.

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:58.560
Turn Up Charlie should turn up on Netflix
in late 2018 or 2019.

